Specification data
------------------

records/annexh.yaml holds the translation of M-Bus data records to OBIS
codes of EN 13757-3:2025 annex H as facts (medium, quantity, modifiers,
storage, OBIS value groups, with the table rows each rule stands for),
written against this package's own quantity names. records/vif_tables.go
holds the VIF and VIFE codes of EN 13757-3:2025 clause 6.4 with names
and units in our own words. No text of the standards is reproduced, and
none of them is redistributed. See PROVENANCE.md.

Meter drivers and receiver sticks
---------------------------------

The meters package reads manufacturers' payload layouts, and
wireless/stick.go speaks receiver sticks' command interfaces. Both are
written from facts (byte positions, scales, bit meanings, command and
mode codes); some of those
facts were read from wmbusmeters (https://github.com/wmbusmeters/
wmbusmeters, GPL-3.0-or-later) and from the makers' documents, as
PROVENANCE.md lists. No manufacturer keys are included: callers
supply them. No code, grammar, table or text of wmbusmeters is
included, and none of its test telegrams is kept in this repository (the
interop tests fetch them at run time).

